  "_description": "Dataset for E6-tool-selection (app/evals/plan.py). Owner: platform (James). Since 2026-09-15/16 two agents SELECT tools at runtime (Care-Routing's ReAct loop; the Reflection critic through the registry gateway), and every agent still declares a static least-privilege TOOL_ALLOWLIST enforced by enforce_tool_access() at the call site. So 'selection accuracy' is not measurable and the evaluation is REFRAMED as enforcement: this is the full (agent, tool) permission matrix. Every permitted pair must execute; every forbidden pair must raise ToolAccessError. When you add a tool to an agent, add its row here — a forbidden pair that silently starts passing is a least-privilege breach (OWASP LLM06/LLM08, FR-12).\n\nThe `route` and `aggregate` pseudo-tools belong to the ORCHESTRATION role, which moved from the platform-owned Supervisor onto Symptom-Intake. Intake is granted both; every other worker is explicitly DENIED both, which is the half that matters — least privilege here means no worker can sequence the pipeline just because it is on the bus.",
